                <pb facs="0701" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg507"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—No official record of the substance of the conversation at this meeting has been
                    found. Byrnes makes the following
                    reference to the meeting in <hi rendition="#italic">Speaking Frankly</hi>, page
                    84: “As soon as Mr. Attlee and Mr.
                        Bevin returned I visited them and,
                    after several hours discussion, obtained their agreement in principle to our
                    proposal [on reparations from Germany].” It seems probable from the minutes of
                    the Byrnes-Molotov meeting and the Tenth Meeting of the Foreign Ministers
                    on July 30 (<hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg481">pages
                        481</ref>, <ref target="#pg484">484</ref>–<ref target="#pg487">487</ref>)
                    that Byrnes’ discussions with the British
                    representatives took place at some time following adjournment of the latter
                    meeting, although the chronology of events described in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Speaking Frankly</hi>, page 84, would indicate that the Byrnes–Attlee meeting took place on July 28.</p>
            </div>
